From e1f04a85f69fb7d2fe09f79b311167a3a3dbfd6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 11:45:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - isolate streaming DMA cache lines

Checking word-aligned addresses and cipher-block lengths is insufficient
for streaming DMA on a non-coherent device. Independent requests may
share a cache line, and cleaning it for one request can overwrite data
already written by the engine for another request. kTLS can pack records
into adjacent page fragments.

DMA_BOUNCE_UNALIGNED_KMALLOC protects small destination mappings, including
the generic GCM mask block. It does not check pointer alignment and skips
mappings at least twice ARCH_DMA_MINALIGN in size. A page-sized SG entry
at a partial cache-line offset can therefore still be mapped directly.

Require cache-aligned offsets and complete SG-entry lengths before using
the direct DMA path. Check the entire mapped entry even when cryptlen
ends before its end. Use the existing bounce path otherwise, and round
its private mapping up to a cache-line boundary without changing the
number of bytes encrypted or copied back.

This fixes an unsafe mapping accepted by the driver. It is a candidate
for the intermittent TLS 1.2 plaintext mismatch seen on AN7581; device
validation is still needed to establish whether it explains that report.

Signed-off-by: Qingfang Deng <dqfext@gmail.com>
---
 eip93-common.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/eip93-common.c b/eip93-common.c
index d23e2cf..462d1a5 100644
--- a/eip93-common.c
+++ b/eip93-common.c
@@ -196,7 +196,8 @@ static int eip93_make_sg_copy(struct scatterlist *src, struct scatterlist **dst,
 	}
 
 	sg_init_table(*dst, 1);
-	sg_set_buf(*dst, pages, len);
+	/* The page allocation owns the padding through the last cache line. */
+	sg_set_buf(*dst, pages, ALIGN(len, dma_get_cache_alignment()));
 
 	/* copy only as requested */
 	if (copy)
@@ -208,12 +209,22 @@ static int eip93_make_sg_copy(struct scatterlist *src, struct scatterlist **dst,
 static bool eip93_is_sg_aligned(struct scatterlist *sg, u32 len,
 				const int blksize)
 {
+	unsigned int dma_align = dma_get_cache_alignment();
 	int nents;
 
 	for (nents = 0; sg; sg = sg_next(sg), ++nents) {
 		if (!IS_ALIGNED(sg->offset, 4))
 			return false;
 
+		/*
+		 * Adjacent requests must not share a streaming DMA cache line.
+		 * dma_map_sg() maps the entire entry, including any bytes beyond
+		 * the requested crypt length in the last entry.
+		 */
+		if (!IS_ALIGNED(sg->offset, dma_align) ||
+		    !IS_ALIGNED(sg->length, dma_align))
+			return false;
+
 		if (len <= sg->length) {
 			if (!IS_ALIGNED(len, blksize))
 				return false;
